# Ember — the environment variables Ember actually reads (E-033)
#
# Ember does NOT load a .env file itself. These variables only
# count when they are set in Ember's real environment — for
# example exported in your shell, or set in the EnvironmentFile=
# of a systemd unit. This file is documentation, nothing more:
# it lists EVERY environment variable the Ember core reads.
# There are exactly two. (Checked against the code in E-013 and
# re-checked in E-033; a variable not listed here is not read,
# whatever older Runa-era documents may claim.)
#
# Ember's settings otherwise live in ONE config file:
# ~/.ember/config/ember.yaml (or ember.toml) — see
# config/ember.example.yaml for every key in plain words.
#
# Rules:
#   - Never commit real values. The repository's .gitignore
#     excludes .env files.
#   - Never put a secret in the config file. The one secret
#     below travels by environment only.
#   - Rotate any value that has been exposed in a screenshot,
#     chat, or PR immediately.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Where your local model program (Ollama) lives
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# OLLAMA_HOST=http://127.0.0.1:11434
#   Optional. Points Ember at Ollama when it is not at the usual
#   place. Also moves the embedding endpoint to match. Accepts
#   host, host:port, or a full http(s) URL. Unset → Ember uses
#   the base_url from the config file (default
#   http://localhost:11434).

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The shared-Well password (only for a pgvector Well)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# EMBER_WELL_PASSWORD=
#   Only needed when your config file selects the pgvector
#   Well (brunnr.backend: pgvector) — a Well shared with other
#   machines. It is checked FIRST, before the computer's
#   keyring and before the mode-600 password file named by the
#   config's secret_ref. The config file can rename this
#   variable (secret_env) — the value itself never goes in any
#   file Ember reads. Leave unset for the normal local Well.
